content.problemStatement:
You receive a 2D matrix `grid` of size `3 x 3` consisting only of characters `'B'` and `'W'`. Character `'W'` represents the white color, and character `'B'` represents the black color.

The task is to change the color of **no more than one** cell so that the matrix has a `2 x 2` square where all cells are of the same color.

Output `true` if it is possible to create a `2 x 2` square of the same color, otherwise, output `false`.

.grid-container {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: 30px 30px 30px;
padding: 10px;
}
.grid-item {
background-color: black;
border: 1px solid gray;
height: 30px;
font-size: 30px;
text-align: center;
}
.grid-item-white {
background-color: white;
}

**Example 1:**

**Input:** grid = [["B","W","B"],["B","W","W"],["B","W","B"]]

**Output:** true

**Explanation:**

It can be done by changing the color of the `grid[0][2]`.

**Example 2:**

**Input:** grid = [["B","W","B"],["W","B","W"],["B","W","B"]]

**Output:** false

**Explanation:**

It cannot be done by changing no more than one cell.

**Example 3:**

**Input:** grid = [["B","W","B"],["B","W","W"],["B","W","W"]]

**Output:** true

**Explanation:**

The `grid` already includes a `2 x 2` square of the same color.

**Constraints:**

* `grid.length == 3`
* `grid[i].length == 3`
* `grid[i][j]` is either `'W'` or `'B'`.

